- [ ] Containerise `ctester-tests` -- the ONLY systemd unit that can be. It
      pulls the private test repo and republishes the catalogue: no root, no
      Docker socket, no host access. The other two must STAY on the host, and
      the reason is worth keeping: `ctester-runner@` is root and drives
      Docker+gVisor (containerising it means docker-in-docker, i.e. handing the
      sandbox the socket it exists to be isolated from), and `ctester-pull`
      restarts the containers -- it cannot live inside one it restarts.
